  "2026-08-23T06:39:18.191Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-23: live GH-1095 reproduced the residual exactly: the 2026.8.23 tag exists, GitHub/npm artifacts do not, npm publish returned E404, and the alert still emitted failing_stage=unrecorded. This tranche extends the existing structured recorder across downstream publish and verification stages without log-text classification."
  "2026-08-23T07:03:27.150Z","harness:codex","Progress: Auto Release now records downstream GitHub Release failures from structured run/job/step conclusions and records discovery/GitHub Release/npm verification stages before exiting; the current npm publish incident would resolve to release-workflow plus Build, Test, Publish / Publish to npm instead of unrecorded."
  "2026-08-23T07:10:42.447Z","harness:codex","Focused verification: release-failure record and CI workflow contract suites passed 37/37; structured negative controls classify only GitHub job/step conclusions and preserve preflight fallback when no record exists."
  "2026-08-23T08:42:01.480Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: exact full-source coverage passed 100/100/100/100; workflow failure recording is covered through structured job/step, sparse, malformed, stage, and negative-control inputs; lint, package, secrets, docs, generated-surface, and live repository assurance gates passed."
  "2026-08-23T08:50:10.880Z","harness:codex","Reviewed delivery: PR #1096 https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1096 carries the structured Auto Release failure record, negative controls, generated changelog entry, and workflow contract proof."
  "2026-08-23T08:59:59.102Z","harness:codex","Hosted static remediation: CI correctly rejected closure without post-epoch defect taxonomy. Classified the escaped release-alert behavior as production_defect and bound it to strengthened gate auto-release-structured-failure-cause with verdict-changing and missing-record negative controls. Windows independently exposed status 2 in the same-day shell simulation; the assertion now includes captured stdout/stderr so any recurrence is actionable rather than opaque."
  "2026-08-23T09:12:49.247Z","harness:codex","Windows root cause and fix: the expanded Auto Release step exceeded the Windows command-line transport ceiling when the acceptance harness passed it through bash -c, truncating the script at line 144 inside a quoted string. The harness now sends identical Bash source over stdin, removing argv-length dependence while preserving the production script and fake-command environment."
  "2026-08-23T10:17:06.128Z","harness:codex","Review remediation evidence: CodeRabbit findings 3838168889, 3838168890, and 3838168891 are addressed by reopening the item, claiming it before edits, linking the cross-platform release-automation contract test before closure, and rerunning the evidence. release-failure-record, CI workflow, and release-automation focused tests passed 24/24. Full coverage passed 7,845 tests across 566 files at exact 100% statements, branches, functions, and lines. pnpm lint and pnpm quality:static passed."
  "2026-08-23T11:06:57.286Z","harness:codex","Exact-head review remediation evidence: CodeRabbit finding 3838291644 is addressed at the canonical source. The PM title now states the public outcome, Structured release-failure causes are preserved in blocked-release alerts, so generated release notes no longer expose internal incident wording. CHANGELOG.md is linked as reviewed documentation. The final focused, TypeScript, static, lint, grammar, generated-surface, and exact-coverage gates pass."
  "2026-08-23T11:32:42.551Z","harness:codex","Review recurrence start: terminal CodeRabbit finding 3838390701 is accepted; preserve the original downstream Release watcher status through all Auto Release caller exits."
  "2026-08-23T11:54:36.145Z","harness:codex","Terminal review remediation evidence: CodeRabbit finding 3838390701 is addressed at all three Auto Release watcher callers. Each now propagates the original gh run watch status while the structured recorder retains the same status, and the workflow contract asserts exactly three preserving calls. Focused release/CI tests pass within 189/189; full coverage is exact across 7,847 tests, and lint/static assurance pass."
  "2026-08-23T12:34:40.249Z","harness:codex","Review recurrence start: CodeRabbit finding 3838502159 is accepted after live validation; blank and whitespace-only workflow statuses must remain unreported rather than normalize to zero."
  "2026-08-23T13:11:31.635Z","harness:codex","Final review evidence: integerStatus now rejects empty and whitespace-only workflow statuses instead of coercing them to zero; unit negative controls cover both forms. Focused release-failure tests, pnpm lint/static assurance, and final exact coverage all pass: 566 files, 7,848 tests, 100/100/100/100."
